The Flex-based single cell RNA-seq raw fastq files were processed with the Costalab scrna_seurat_pipeline (https://github.com/CostaLab/scrna_seurat_pipeline.git). We ran the pipeline in a local singularity container. The script and parameters are shown below.  
```
#!/bin/bash

### Job name
#SBATCH -J kidney12_scRNA

### Set logs, remember to create logs dir
#SBATCH -e logs/error.%j.%x.txt
#SBATCH -o logs/output.%j.%x.txt

### Time to execute, e. g. 15 min 30 sec
#SBATCH -t 72:00:00

### Job memory needs per node, e. g. 1 GB
#SBATCH --mem=400G

### OpenMP threads
#SBATCH --cpus-per-task=24

### Account
#SBATCH --account=p0020567
################################################################
# PATH
#if [ -r /usr/local_host/etc/bashrc ]; then
#   . /usr/local_host/etc/bashrc
#fi

#export PATH=/usr/bin:$PATH
#export PATH=/usr/local_host/bin:$PATH
################################################################
#module load scRNA
#source ~/miniconda3/bin/activate
#conda activate Seurat3
################################################################

# could also define it here instead of taking it as an arg
proj_name="kidney11"
# data dir (where your results will be saved)

data_path="/app/scrna_seurat_pipeline_results_3"
#data_path=`pwd`

date
## 50 cores run, future memory
#mkdir -p ${data_path}/${proj_name}
#ln -s ${data_path}/conf/config_${proj_name}.R ${data_path}/${proj_name}
apptainer exec -w --bind /hpcwork/p0020567/data/dbit-seq/scRNA_data:/app /hpcwork/fp015734/Software/packages/scrna_pipeline_docker /usr/bin/Rscript /app/scrna_seurat_pipeline/data_factory.R -n 24 --MaxMemMega=180000 -z "lz4" -c "/app/scrna_seurat_pipeline/conf/config_kidney7.R" -s "${data_path}/${proj_name}/save" -e "${data_path}/${proj_name}/charts" -a seurat_clusters --allinone=TRUE --nFeatureRNAfloor=400 --nCountRNAfloor=500 --nCountRNAceiling=20000 --pct_mitoceiling=10 --pct_riboceiling=100 --countmatrixformat='10X' --dims4Integrate="1:30" --Dims4FindNeighbors="1:50" --harmony_dim="1:50" -r 1.5

date
```
After finishing the above pipeline, we first annotate the scRNA-seq results and then integrate the data with Spatial ATAC-seq data for annotation.


